{"skill":{"slug":"web-search-exa","displayName":"Web Search by Exa"},"version":{"version":"2.0.0","createdAt":1773248698117,"changelog":"Major update: covers all 9 MCP tools, adds YAML frontmatter, query tips, category filters, structured extraction, deep research, token efficiency","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":11769,"sha256":"24f08ac90b30a09898db6b6b7be6a45e449015e378cf5b9b132756ee25c1c88b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2391,"sha256":"9159b3cc5d93b11e7bf2bffbd66d6c0e18485b4616ceacd70fd631b5016e6557","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789021485660,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"3ee460945f4064b7d0363042d562b91c83fc8c6fbfaa50e3eb9ab3dd83556b1d","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/3ee460945f4064b7d0363042d562b91c83fc8c6fbfaa50e3eb9ab3dd83556b1d","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: web-search-exa\nVersion: 2.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is a legitimate integration for the Exa neural web search engine via the Model Context Protocol (MCP). The documentation in SKILL.md correctly describes web search, content extraction, and research capabilities using the official Exa MCP server (mcp.exa.ai), with no evidence of malicious instructions, data exfiltration, or unauthorized execution logic.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160048068},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":14,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789021485660},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"The skill is a coherent Exa web-search MCP integration, but its setup encourages API keys in URLs and its people-search examples lack privacy guardrails.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The artifact contains only Markdown instructions and no local executable code; network use through Exa is expected for the purpose, but returned web/profile data may include personal information.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Installation is a normal MCP URL registration, but optional paid/authenticated setup instructs users to place the Exa API key directly in the endpoint query string.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill clearly scopes itself to web search and retrieval, but it promotes people/profile discovery and LinkedIn-style searches without acceptable-use, consent, or privacy guidance.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No local persistence, privilege escalation, tool hijacking, or background service is present in the artifact; the main durable state is the MCP server configuration that may contain a credential-bearing URL.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The documented capabilities match the stated purpose: web search, URL crawling, code/context lookup, company research, people search, and Exa-hosted deep research.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. Use the unauthenticated MCP URL where possible, avoid storing an Exa API key directly in a shared URL or config, rotate any key that has been exposed in logs or screenshots, and use people/profile search only for legitimate, authorized public research with appropriate privacy and platform-term checks.","findings":"[T09] unexpected: Accepted in context: authentication to Exa is purpose-aligned, but documenting the API key as a URL query parameter is an avoidable credential exposure risk and is not accompanied by safer handling guidance.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: Accepted in context for the credential-handling concern: the artifact explicitly shows exaApiKey in MCP URL examples, which may be stored or logged by client configuration paths.\n[SQP-2] expected: Partially accepted in context for people search: finding professionals and profiles is disclosed and purpose-aligned, but the artifact does not provide privacy or acceptable-use boundaries for collecting or enriching personal profile data.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789021485660}}}}}